  "{:catalog-home \"com-etzhayyim-gtin (4 collection: product/alias/brand/category, DID did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:gtin)\", :gtin.category \"UNSPSC metadata mirror — SSoT is kotoba-lang/unspsc, no full segment->family->class->commodity tree on the gtin side (ADR-2607031800 category-as-metadata-only); commodity parentId points at segment, family/class honestly :missing-family-class\", :check-digit \"spec-faithful (GS1 mod-10) cljs/nbb-portable port of uchiwake_edn.cljc:150-179 into src/gtin/identifier.cljc — standalone contract forbids requiring uchiwake, but the GS1 spec is fixed so both agree on every valid/invalid code\", :generator \"scripts/build_catalog.cljc integrates uchiwake seed+merged + kotoba-lang/unspsc registry.edn -> data/{product,alias,brand,category}.edn (dev-time superproject path refs; runtime reads only the committed data/*.edn, keeping standalone contract)\", :external-sources \"OpenFoodFacts first-class (CC-BY-SA, no auth) + GS1/UNSPSC official operator-gated (Phase 4B R0 stub, credential tool only — no AI form-input, safety floor 1)\", :cloud-itonami \"dual-source: import-gtin-catalog! preferred -> import-uchiwake-seed! -> coverage fixture (backward-compatible; standalone/CI with no orgs/ tree falls through to uchiwake/fixture exactly as before)\", :sourcing-honesty \"every row carries :*/sourcing in #{:authoritative :representative :synthesized} (uchiwake G5 carry-through)\", :artifacts {\"com-etzhayyim-gtin\" \"e3b9376 (PR #3, 29 tests/384 assertions)\", \"cloud-itonami\" \"f43c499 (PR #451, portable-cljs 427 tests/4824 assertions)\"}}"
  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607182100: GTIN actor catalog + UNSPSC bridge — canonical product identity, dual-source cloud-itonami\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nThe GTIN actor (`com-etzhayyim-gtin`) shipped as design-only: `manifest.edn`, `CLAUDE.md` (4-collection data model, DID patterns, path-resolve priority), and `openapi/gtin.openapi.json` (the `validateGtin`/`lookupProduct`/`registerProduct` XRPC surface) — but **no catalog data and no methods implementation** (0% implemented). The GTIN↔UNSPSC connection was carried entirely by `uchiwake`'s `data/seed-products.kotoba.edn`, which `cloud-itonami`'s `product_party.cljc` imported by **file path directly** (`import-uchiwake-seed!`), not through any actor contract. `mamori.cljc` recorded this gap verbatim: *\"no etzhayyim actor endpoint was confirmed to exist\"*.\n\nThe GS1 mod-10 check-digit / GTIN-14 normalize logic already existed in `uchiwake/methods/uchiwake_edn.cljc`, but the GTIN actor's **standalone repository contract** (`bb run_tests.clj` must pass from a standalone checkout, superproject-independent — CLAUDE.md L149-156) forbids requiring `uchiwake` (a sibling repo). So the SSoT delegate was hollow: the design pointed at a GTIN actor that had no code and no data.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Catalog home = `com-etzhayyim-gtin` (4 collection)\n\nThe canonical product-identity catalog lives in the GTIN actor itself: `data/{product,alias,brand,category}.edn`, keyed by the new DID scheme `did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:gtin` (`identity.edn` is the actor root; the legacy `did:web:gtin.etzhayyim.com` is retained as `:actor/legacy-did`). Collection shapes follow CLAUDE.md: `gtin.product (productId,gtin,jan,upc,ean,name,brand,model,packSize,category)`, `gtin.alias (canonicalProductId,codeType,codeValue)`, `gtin.brand (brandId,name,ownerDid,country)`, `gtin.category (categoryId,name,parentId)`.\n\n### 2. `gtin.category` is an UNSPSC **metadata mirror**, not a tree\n\nGTIN is an identifier system, not a classification taxonomy (ADR-2607031800). The `gtin.category` collection carries commodity codes as metadata only: a commodity (8-digit) node's `parentId` points at its segment (2-digit), with `:status :missing-family-class` honestly noting the absent family/class layers. The **full segment→family→class→commodity tree stays in `kotoba-lang/unspsc`** (the SSoT); the GTIN actor never reconstructs it. Segment resolution at runtime goes through `gtin.identifier/unspsc-segment` (mirrors `kotoba.unspsc.product/unspsc-segment`).\n\n### 3. Check-digit ported spec-faithfully into `src/gtin/identifier.cljc`\n\n`normalize-gtin` / `gtin-check-digit-ok` are a GS1 mod-10 spec-faithful re-implementation of `uchiwake_edn.cljc:150-179`, written cljs/nbb-portable (no `Character`/`.charAt` interop). The standalone contract forbids `require`-ing uchiwake, but the GS1 algorithm is a fixed spec, so both implementations agree on every valid/invalid code — verified by `gtin.identifier-test` with known public GS1 vectors (Coca-Cola 5449000000996, Nutella 3017620422003, JAN 4902102139496, GTIN-14 00194253396062).\n\n### 4. Generator reads superproject at dev-time, runtime reads only `data/*.edn`\n\n`scripts/build_catalog.cljc` integrates `uchiwake` seed+merged EDN and `kotoba-lang/unspsc` `registry.edn` to emit the 4-collection catalog. It references superproject-relative paths **only at generation time**; the runtime (and the standalone test suite) reads only the committed `data/*.edn`, preserving the standalone contract.\n\n### 5. External sources: OpenFoodFacts first-class, GS1/UNSPSC operator-gated\n\nOpenFoodFacts (CC-BY-SA, no auth) is a first-class ingest source via the existing uchiwake adapter. GS1 GEPIR and the official UNSPSC codeset (family/class gap-fill) are operator-gated (`UCHIWAKE_OPERATOR_GATE`-equivalent threshold, uchiwake G7) and loaded from a credential-tool-supplied cache — an AI agent never form-inputs credentials (safety floor 1). Phase 4B ships these as R0 stubs.\n\n### 6. cloud-itonami dual-source (backward-compatible)\n\n`product_party.cljc` gains `import-gtin-catalog!` (+ reverse-map `gtin-product->uchiwake`, `default-gtin-catalog-candidates`, `resolve-gtin-catalog-path`); `bootstrap-join!` :clj base now tries **gtin-catalog → uchiwake-seed → coverage-fixture**. In standalone/CI (no `orgs/` tree) the gtin catalog resolves nil and bootstrap falls through to uchiwake/fixture exactly as before; in the superproject layout the canonical gtin catalog wins. `gtin_client.cljc` is the file-based client boundary now; it becomes the XRPC client once `gtin.etzhayyim.com` deploys (Phase 6, separate ADR — the `mamori.cljc` note flips then).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) The GTIN actor ships a real catalog and XRPC-shaped methods; the SSoT delegate is no longer hollow.\n- (+) cloud-itonami consumes the canonical product-identity surface through a named client boundary instead of a raw uchiwake seed path.\n- (+) Sourcing honesty carries through (every row `:*/sourcing`); the standalone contract is preserved (no uchiwake `require`).\n- (−) `:clj` test-jvm in cloud-itonami is blocked by a pre-existing `kotoba.plm.routing` classpath gap unrelated to this change (not a hook gate); the :clj reverse-map logic mirrors the gtin-actor-side mapping validated by com-etzhayyim-gtin's 29-test suite. Follow-up: fix the plm routing classpath.\n- (−) Live XRPC (`gtin.etzhayyim.com` deploy) is out of scope; Phase 5 is file-based. The dual-source design keeps the call-site stable across both phases.\n- (−) UNSPSC family/class (4/6-digit) layers remain absent fleet-wide (only segment 2-digit + commodity 8-digit exist); honest `:missing-family-class` until the operator-gated official codeset lands (Phase 4B).\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-gtin@e3b9376` — PR #3 (catalog + methods + identifier; 29 tests / 384 assertions green, `bb run_tests.clj` standalone)\n- `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami@f43c499` — PR #451 (dual-source import + gtin_client; portable-cljs 427 tests / 4824 assertions green)\n- manifest pin advanced: `com-etzhayyim-gtin` 199e1b3 → e3b9376 (superproject `eb12f4a`); cloud-itonami tracks `revision: main`\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607031800 — cloud-itonami-gtin functional blueprints (GTIN is an identifier system, not a classification taxonomy; category-as-metadata-only)\n- ADR-2607031700 — cloud-itonami-unspsc-commodity-segment-blueprints\n- ADR-2800000000 — cloud-itonami-unspsc-gtin-linkage (ISIC-actor-local UNSPSC/GTIN placeholder fields; complementary, not overlapping)\n- ADR-2607171600 — docs/ADR EDN-only + DataScript query\n- `uchiwake` CLAUDE.md — G1/G5/G7 sourcing honesty + operator gate\n"}]
